   "content": "PolyStrata is a local inference engine for Qwen3.8-Flash-Next, a large language model with a mixture-of-experts architecture. It runs on a single GPU (NVIDIA RTX 20\u201350 series or supported AMD cards) with 12 GB or more of VRAM, and requires 64 GB of system RAM for the full models. The model's experts are split between the GPU and the CPU: the most frequently used experts are cached in VRAM, while the rest are computed on the CPU or streamed over PCIe. An expert profile ranks all 24,576 experts by usage so the cache adapts to the conversation.\n\nThree quantized model sizes are offered: Q2_0 (66 GB download, ~34 GB of experts in RAM, fastest), IQ2_XS (68 GB, ~36 GB, slightly better quality at close speed), and IQ3_XXS (76 GB, ~43 GB, best quality but slower due to more CPU work). A pruned \"Coder\" variant keeps only 256 of each layer's 512 experts, runs on 32 GB of RAM, and retains 91.3% of the full model's SWE-bench Verified score. A fine-tune called Swift 1.5 produces answers with roughly 63% fewer thinking tokens at under 1% accuracy loss. An experimental 4-bit quantization (Unsloth UD-Q4_K_XL, 111 GB) runs at 7\u20138.5 tokens/s on a 64 GB PC by reading most experts from the SSD.\n\nOn the reference machine (RTX 5070 12 GB, Ryzen 5 7600, 64 GB DDR5), Q2_0 processes a 4K-token prompt at about 1,299 tokens/s and generates output at roughly 93 tokens/s; at 128K context, prompt speed drops to about 2,100 tokens/s and output to 74 tokens/s. Engine 0.1.36 improved prompt speed by 16\u201322% with fused int8 tensor-core kernels and output speed by 5\u201318% with thread-block-cluster decode kernels on RTX 50 series cards. Time to first token is about 4 seconds at 4K, 25 seconds at 32K, and under 2 minutes at 128K.\n\nSeveral memory-management features extend what is possible on limited hardware. KV streaming (engine 0.1.5) keeps the context's KV cache in RAM and streams only the portion attention needs into VRAM, freeing space for more experts; at 262K context this raised Q2_0 output from 50.9 to 62.6 tokens/s. A 4-bit KV cache option halves KV memory at a small quality cost. A hybrid K8V4 format keeps keys at 8 bits and values at 4 bits, saving 23% of KV memory. Low-RAM mode (engine 0.1.26) maps experts from a file on disk instead of copying them all into RAM, reducing committed memory from 36 GB to about 13 GB on the Coder model. A resident variant (0.1.30) copies only the experts the GPU does not hold into pinned RAM, avoiding SSD reads during",
